      "title": "Meta's Muse AI agent can book, buy, and browse for you: Here's how it works",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/technology/tech-news/meta-muse-ai-agent-book-buy-work-how-it-works-126090900322_1.html",
      "description": "Meta's Muse is a personal AI agent that can browse the web, book travel, send emails, make purchases and continue working on tasks in the background, while asking users to approve sensitive actions",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-09T05:30:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "Meta launches personal AI agent 'Muse' to help with everyday tasks",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/technology/artificial-intelligence/meta-launches-personal-ai-agent-muse-to-help-with-everyday-tasks-126090900039_1.html",
      "description": "Meta launched on Tuesday a personal artificial intelligence agent, Muse, for people 18 and over who are looking for help with day-to-day tasks like schedules, shopping and, in the company's words, turning \"long-term goals into action plans.\"\nThe parent company of Instagram and Facebook is stressing the safety and privacy features of the agent, which for now is only available in the US Muse, Meta said, runs on a dedicated, secure virtual machine that houses both the agent and the user's data.\nPeople can message the agent in a separate app, called Muse, or message it in WhatsApp. It can handle simple tasks like sending an email or booking travel, or bigger, long-term goals like creating a yearlong exercise plan or setting up a new business.\n\"Once a person shares a goal with Muse, it helps them develop a personalised plan and coordinate their time and resources, then advances the work on its own. It can open a browser, fill out forms, and negotiate on their behalf,\" Meta said in a blog",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-09T02:44:51"
    },
    {
      "title": "Meta’s stock jumps as new personal AI agent Muse addresses a major investor concern",
